---
import CalculatorLayout from '@/layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro'
import { getToolBySlug, getCategoryBySlug } from '@/data/tools'
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content'
import { RothIRACalculator } from '@/components/calculators/roth-ira-calculator/index.tsx'

const tool = getToolBySlug('roth-ira-calculator')!
const category = getCategoryBySlug(tool.category)!
const entry = await getEntry('tools', 'roth-ira-calculator')
const { data } = entry!
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title={`${tool.name} - Tax-Free Retirement Growth | FinCalc Pro`}
  description={data.description}
  toolName={tool.name}
  category={tool.category}
  categoryName={category.name}
  toolDescription={data.description}
  faqs={data.faqs}
  relatedSlug={tool.slug}
  taxYear="2026"
>
  <div slot="calculator">
    <RothIRACalculator client:load />
  </div>
  <p slot="intro" class="text-muted-foreground mb-8">
    A <strong>Roth IRA calculator</strong> shows you the remarkable power of tax-free growth. Unlike Traditional IRAs, Roth contributions grow tax-free and qualified withdrawals in retirement are completely tax-free.
  </p>
  <div slot="how-to-use">
    <p>Enter your current age, current Roth IRA balance, and how much you plan to contribute annually (up to the $7,000 limit for 2026). Set your expected annual return and target retirement age. Click Calculate to see your projected balance at retirement, the total contributions you made, and the tax-free earnings your money generated.</p>
  </div>
  <div slot="formula">
    <p>The Roth IRA projection uses the same future value formula as other investment calculators:</p>
    <p class="font-mono text-sm bg-muted p-3 rounded">FV = P × (1 + r/n)^(n×t) + PMT × [ ((1 + r/n)^(n×t) − 1) / (r/n) ]</p>
    <p>The difference is in the tax treatment, not the math. Contributions are made after-tax (no deduction now), but all growth and qualified withdrawals are entirely tax-free. The calculator applies the annual contribution limit ($7,000 for 2026, or $8,000 with catch-up for age 50+).</p>
  </div>
</CalculatorLayout>
